Subject: [DRAFT / SKETCH] AI COLUMN: parser surface for "AI COLUMN (expr) WITH (...)" and "RETRY AI COLUMN"

*** THIS IS A DESIGN SKETCH, NOT AN APPLICABLE PATCH. ***
It will not apply cleanly and nothing in it has been compiled or bison-checked.
It is here because the grammar surface is fully determined by the shipped tests
and because reading the parser revealed three concrete gotchas that are easy to
miss (keyword RETRY does not exist; AI COLUMN must ride the existing generated
column shape; ALTER actions are merged by node type).  Everything marked PROVEN
was read off origin/2026-competition; everything else needs the implementer's
decision on the Linux box.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1) Keyword situation (PROVEN, and this is the first thing to fix)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * AI is already a non-reserved keyword: token list
    src/sql/parser/sql_parser_mysql_mode.y:262, keyword alternatives at :16440
    ("| AI { make_name_node(..., \"ai\"); }") and :17500 ("| AI" inside the
    unreserved_keyword list), table entry in
    src/sql/parser/non_reserved_keywords_mysql_mode.c.
  * COLUMN already exists as a keyword (reserved list, .y:227).
  * **RETRY does not exist as a token.** `grep -n RETRY sql_parser_mysql_mode.y`
    only matches the compound MASTER_* keywords at :309-310.  So adding
    `ALTER TABLE ... RETRY AI COLUMN` requires all three of:
      a. `RETRY` token declaration in the %token block (starts .y:60 ff),
      b. `{"retry", RETRY}` in non_reserved_keywords_mysql_mode.c (alphabetical
         neighbours: :683 "reverse", :688 "role", :689 "rollback"),
      c. `| RETRY` in the unreserved_keyword list (near .y:17500).
    Then re-check tools/deploy/mysql_test/t/non_reserved_keyword.test (only 26
    lines, does not enumerate AI/COLUMN today) so the new keyword does not turn
    a green case red.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2) Column definition shape to copy (PROVEN)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The nearest existing rule, .y:4843 (generated columns), already threads
"column name + data type + expression + attributes" through T_COLUMN_DEFINITION
with 7 children:

  | column_definition_ref data_type opt_collation opt_generated_keyname
      AS '(' expr ')' opt_storage_type opt_generated_column_attribute_list
      opt_column_reference opt_position_column
    { ... malloc_non_terminal_node($$, result->malloc_pool_,
          T_COLUMN_DEFINITION, 7, $1, $2, attributes, $7, $9, $12, $4); }

`opt_generated_keyname` itself is at .y:4913-4931.  Do NOT silently widen
T_COLUMN_DEFINITION's arity: ob_create_table_resolver.cpp /
ob_alter_table_resolver.cpp index the children positionally.  Prefer a new
non-terminal hanging off the attribute list, or a new item type, and let the
resolver attach the AI column info to the column schema + CreateTableArg.

Needed new item types (next free value is 2087 -- src/objit/include/objit/
common/ob_item_type.h currently ends that block at T_FUN_SYS_BUCKET = 2086,
line 918; confirm nothing above 2086 before taking these):

  T_AI_COLUMN_CLAUSE      /* AI COLUMN ( expr ) WITH ( options ) */
  T_AI_COLUMN_OPTION_LIST /* sync_mode='async', max_retries=N          */
  T_RETRY_AI_COLUMN       /* ALTER TABLE action                        */

Grammar sketch (illustrative only):

--- a/src/sql/parser/sql_parser_mysql_mode.y
+++ b/src/sql/parser/sql_parser_mysql_mode.y
@@ column_definition (existing alternatives around line 4843)
+| column_definition_ref data_type opt_collation
+  AI COLUMN '(' expr ')' WITH '(' ai_column_option_list ')'
+{
+  /* Same 7-child T_COLUMN_DEFINITION as the generated-column rule, with the
+   * AI clause hung on as an extra attribute node so positional consumers are
+   * untouched.  set_data_type_collation()/dup_expr_string() calls mirror the
+   * generated-column rule at :4843-4850 because the expression text must be
+   * preserved verbatim: ai_column_ddl.test:72-78 asserts on normalized_expr,
+   * which is produced from this node's printed form plus the result-type
+   * prompt. */
+  ParseNode *attributes = NULL;
+  set_data_type_collation($2, $3, true, false);
+  dup_expr_string($6, result, @6.first_column, @6.last_column);
+  ParseNode *ai_clause = NULL;
+  malloc_non_terminal_node(ai_clause, result->malloc_pool_, T_AI_COLUMN_CLAUSE,
+                           2, $6, $9);
+  merge_nodes(attributes, result, T_COLUMN_ATTRIBUTES, ai_clause);
+  malloc_non_terminal_node($$, result->malloc_pool_, T_COLUMN_DEFINITION, 7,
+                           $1, $2, attributes, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
+}
+;
+
+ai_column_option_list:
+  ai_column_option
+| ai_column_option_list ',' ai_column_option
+;
+
+ai_column_option:
+  RELATION_NAME opt_equal_mark STRING_VALUE   /* sync_mode = 'async'   */
+| RELATION_NAME opt_equal_mark INTNUM         /* max_retries = N       */
+;
+
+/* Required by the tests verbatim:
+ *   WITH (sync_mode='async', max_retries=2)      -- ai_column_ddl.test:33
+ *   WITH (sync_mode='async', max_retries=3)      -- ai_column_ddl.test:36
+ * Only these two options appear anywhere in the shipped cases; unknown option
+ * names and sync_mode='sync' must be rejected in the resolver (the题面 limits
+ * this task to async).
+ */

@@ alter_table_action (rule begins at .y:14694)
+| RETRY AI COLUMN relation_column opt_where_clause_for_retry_ai
+{
+  /* The two negative cases in ai_column_retry_strict.test:175-179 pin the
+   * error surface, and both are OB_NOT_SUPPORTED (-4007 -> mysql errno 1235,
+   * src/share/ob_errno.def:77, user msg template "%s not supported"):
+   *   retry ai column content  -> "retrying a column that is not an AI column"
+   *   retry ai column result where id = 1, add column extra_col int
+   *                            -> "combining AI COLUMN RETRY with another
+   *                               ALTER action"
+   * The second one is enforced in the resolver, not the grammar: alter_table_
+   * action nodes arrive as a list, so count them and reject when a
+   * T_RETRY_AI_COLUMN shares the statement with anything else.
+   * RETRY must target exactly one column and accepts an optional WHERE whose
+   * bare `status` identifier is a *pseudo column* resolved against the AI
+   * state column, while `` `status` `` (backquoted) resolves against the
+   * physical business column of that name -- ai_column_retry_strict.test:114-
+   * 116 vs :170 prove both behaviours on a table that really has a `status`
+   * varchar(20) column (:21).  Preserve the quote-ness of the identifier
+   * through the parse tree (delimited-name flag) so the resolver can tell
+   * them apart; that flag, not the string, is the discriminator.
+   */
+}

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
3) What is deliberately NOT sketched here
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * `SHOW AI COLUMNS` (named in the题面's unittest list, and *not* exercised by
    any shipped mysqltest) -- no grammar evidence to work from.  Because the
    unittest harness is missing entirely (GAP.md §1), this sub-feature has no
    acceptance target at all; implement it only after the 5 shipped cases pass,
    and expect hidden tests there.
  * The ALTER path plumbing (ObAlterTableArg / a new ObAIColumnRetryArg /
    rootserver/ob_ddl_service.cpp entry) -- needs a design decision on whether
    RETRY is a schema operation at all (it is a data operation: it must
    invalidate rows and enqueue tasks, and the tests expect it to be
    transactional with the row state).  Guessing the RPC/arg shape in a patch
    would be worse than leaving it out.
  * Anything touching src/sql/engine/expr/ob_expr_ai/* or
    src/share/ai_service/ob_ai_service_struct.cpp: another agent owns those
    (D:\scratch\ai-fn\, 5 patches).  The type prompt strings
    ("Return exactly one valid JSON value", "base-10 integer") must therefore
    live in the new AI COLUMN module and be injected when the worker builds the
    system message, not by editing AI_COMPLETE's own behaviour.
